  "dom_id": "step-t1501",
  "name": "Decreasing and Strictly Decreasing Functions",
  "problem": "A function $f(x)$ is **strictly decreasing** if its $y$-value always *falls* as we increase the $x$-value. No section of the graph is allowed to be flat.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14192941/assets/b8a2d54cedc84f159a61bfccc11bdab9adc73eb54b694dd1167802998f4d39d3.png)\n\nOn the other hand, a function $f(x)$ is **decreasing** if its $y$-value *never rises* as we increase the $x$-value. Decreasing functions are allowed to have flat sections.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14192941/assets/4f91b34a57ac42ba82e937c78c74bcb26677e1d6fbf8ed40865f6db73b1cf613.png)",
